applications to them for the workspaces, window title and media buttons, as
HyprPanel's built-in table (and the few apps added in its config) did.
Applications HyprPanel had no icon for get Wayle's own (its built-in table,
else its generic icon), so new installs follow Wayle.

Run once after installing (bootstrap does), and again after changing the
tables below. Needs a Nerd Font (Iosevka Nerd Font) and python-fonttools.

Each icon is a 1 em square centred on its glyph, so at an icon size of N px
it is as big as the glyph in N px text (HyprPanel: mostly 16 px).

Also text drawn as icons (TEXT_ICONS), for labels Wayle has built in: the
dashboard's "Night Mode" and "Color Picker" tiles (styles/index.scss,
~/.scripts/night-mode-tile, ~/.scripts/color-picker-tile).
Written as Wayle's tile labels render (Noto Sans SemiBold 13 px, slight
hinting, the baseline on a pixel), so drawn at 1:1 they look the same.
"""
